    <string name="guide_title">Manual load guide</string>
    <string name="guide_summary">Wireless debugging / adb steps to late-load manually</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">If one-tap jailbreak is not available, use wireless debugging (Android 11+) or a USB cable together with your usual temporary-root method, then run late-load.</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_title">Enable wireless debugging and pair</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_body">Developer options -> Wireless debugging -> Pair device with pairing code. Run the command on a PC with adb, replacing IP and port with the ones shown.</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_title">Connect</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_body">Use the wireless debugging port (not the pairing port).</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_title">Get a temporary root shell</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_body">If your ROM allows adb root, run the command below; otherwise use your usual exploit to obtain a root shell.</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_title">Push ksud and late-load</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_body">Extract ksud from the manager APK (lib/arm64-v8a/libksud.so), push it and run late-load with the manager package name.</string>
    <string name="guide_note">After a successful load the manager will be restarted automatically. Ensure the APK that provided ksud is the same version you use as manager.</string>
